error[approx-zero]: `x ≈ 0` is true only when `x == 0`
 --> positive.jl:3:12
  |
3 |     return x ≈ 0
  |            ^^^^^ relative tolerance scales with zero
  |
  = why: `isapprox` defaults to relative tolerance; relative to zero, no nonzero value is close
  = fix: pass absolute tolerance: `isapprox(x, 0; atol = tol)`   [manual]
  = docs: corset explain approx-zero
  = note: deny from correctness group, library preset
  = note: opt out with `# corset: allow approx-zero -- <reason>`

error[approx-zero]: `isapprox(0.0, residual(x))` is true only when `residual(x) == 0`
 --> positive.jl:6:1
